":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**No.** Exchange volume shows only secondary-market trading, not total accessible liquidity.\n\n**Creation/redemption:** Authorized participants (APs) can create ETF shares by delivering the underlying basket (or cash) to the issuer, or redeem shares for the basket. This arbitrage tends to keep prices near NAV and lets supply expand or contract with demand. So an ETF's liquidity depends substantially on the liquidity of its **underlying holdings**, not just its own trading history.\n\n**Additional indicators to examine:**\n- Bid-ask spread (quoted and effective), across the trading day\n- Displayed depth/quote size at the NBBO\n- Premium/discount to NAV/iNAV, and its volatility\n- Underlying securities' volume, spreads and market hours (e.g., foreign or bond markets)\n- Creation unit size, fees and cash vs. in-kind terms\n- Number of active APs and market makers\n- Market conditions and volatility\n\nLarge orders may warrant a liquidity-provider/block desk consultation. None of this guarantees execution at a given size or price.","ttft_ms":1016,"type":"result","duration_ms":5047,"uuid":"12841855-03e8-4054-8c7e-6037626b4f1b","ttft_stream_ms":969,"time_to_request_ms":67,"first_content_frame_ms":969,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
